{"seq":13,"trial_id":"shared-brain-access-2026-11/openclaw-opus-none-mu-v031-dev/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r1","wall_ts":"2026-11-22T12:54:32.020Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"e23a5e0dcc8202818cc04d9927cf2055a8637a14ab655ebba219155d4e0651be","actor":"assistant","via":"mcp","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DSHARED0001","text":"Hi Dana, I went through all six of Moss's digests on the share. Two of them have Quarrendon Freight Lines ticket numbers:\n\n• *#PD-4492*: from \"Moss: Sunday prep for Ruth\" (teams/team-north/digests/2025-10-05-north-sunday.md). Thea Ramaswell opened it on 4 Oct 2025. Drivers checking in at the Eau Claire gatehouse kiosk weren't getting SMS bay assignments for Dock Doors 14–18 on the 04:00 shift. Support patched the SMS routing that evening, and Thea confirmed the 5 Oct shift went through cleanly. The action item was to archive the kiosk logs before the 14 Oct maintenance window.\n• *#4419*: from \"Moss: North cheat sheet (undated)\" (teams/team-north/digests/north-account-cheatsheet.md). Thea logged it because the gatehouse barcode scanners weren't reading trailer tags at Door 14 on third shift. It was escalated to tier-2 for scanner firmware testing. That file has no date.\n\nThe 9/14 pipeline digest and the 3/23 renewal note both mention QFL but don't give a ticket number. The Central digests have tickets #4409 and #4412 and FR-882, but those are for Central accounts, not QFL. Marcus's \"Quarendon Freightways\" note is about a different company that isn't a customer, so I left it out."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DSHARED0001","ts":"1791987000.000124"}}
